From: SORABBYNGO Engineering <kernel@sorabbyngo.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] seccomp: add sorabbyngo pledge-inspired promise sets

Implements a Linux adaptation of OpenBSD's pledge(2). Processes declare
their syscall intentions at startup via prctl(PR_SET_SORABBYNGO_PLEDGE).
The kernel then enforces a seccomp-BPF filter corresponding to that
promise set. Violations send SIGKILL (matching OpenBSD behaviour).

Promise sets implemented:
  stdio    — read, write, close, fstat, exit, sigreturn
  rpath    — open(O_RDONLY), stat, lstat, fstatat, readlink
  wpath    — open(O_WRONLY|O_CREAT), rename, unlink, mkdir
  inet     — socket(AF_INET/AF_INET6), connect, bind, listen
  dns      — socket(AF_INET), sendto, recvfrom, getaddrinfo helpers
  proc     — fork, exec, wait4, getpid, getppid
  id       — getuid, getgid, setuid, setgid
  tty      — ioctl(TIOCGWINSZ), isatty helpers

Byngox agents and Chameha use this at init time to drop unneeded
capabilities before entering their main loop.

Inspired by OpenBSD sys/kern/kern_pledge.c
